# Identity: with mu_K = Khat.qhat, mu_x = e_x.qhat and khat.qhat = c mu_K + s mu_x as in moments.dat, rho = kq,
#   B = -(1/2) K^2 Y_lin_lt and a moment P_j = sum over its lines of coef mu_K^a mu_x^b (moments.dat, degree n),
#     (-i)^(n mod 2) int dOmega/(4 pi) e^(i k.q) e^(B mu_K^2) P_j = sum_L j_L(rho) C_L^j,
#     C_L^j = sum over the lines of P_j of coef sum_r s^r P_L^(r)(c) sum_i T^(a,b,r)_(L,i) J_i(B),
#   J_i(B) = int_{-1}^{1} du P_i(u) e^(B u^2), P_L^(r) the r-th derivative of the Legendre polynomial P_L,
#   r = b, b - 2, .. >= 0 and
#     T^(a,b,r)_(L,i) = phi_L ((2L + 1)/2) kappa_(b,r) (L - r)!/(L + r)! R^(a,b,r)_(L,i),   phi_L = (-1)^floor(L/2),
#   kappa_(b,r) = eps_r 2^-b binom(b, (b - r)/2) (eps_0 = 1, eps_r = 2 for r > 0) and R^(a,b,r)_(L,i) the coefficient
#   of P_i(u) in u^a (1 - u^2)^((b + r)/2) P_L^(r)(u).  From the plane-wave expansion, the addition theorem of P_L and
#   the azimuthal average of cos(r phi) cos^b(phi) (tools/pt_autogen/lpt_legendre.py).  The paper's azimuth phi of q
#   around K has mu_x = -sqrt(1 - mu_K^2) cos phi, so its monomial mu_K^m (sqrt(1 - mu_K^2) cos phi)^n of I_(m,n) is
#   (-1)^n mu_K^m mu_x^n, of type (a, b) = (m, n).
# Band: T is nonzero only for L = a + b mod 2, L >= r, even i and |i - L| <= a + b (asserted).
